<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#cloves">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cloves</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cloves are the aromatic dried flower buds of a tree native to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maluku-islands">Maluku Islands</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>. They were among the most valuable <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spice-trade">spices</a> of the Asian trade. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portuguese-empire">Portuguese Empire</a> and then the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-empire">Dutch Empire</a> competed for control of their production, with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">Dutch East India Company</a> enforcing a strict monopoly.</p></div>
